abstract: "Snake-in-the-Box solver in Python: heuristically pruned breadth-first search with bit-array vertex tracking and lower-dimension priming to find long induced paths in n-dimensional hypercubes, reaching bounds of 732 (11D), 1439 (12D) and 2854 (13D), plus validation, record database and 3D visualization."
